+## ITM-01/02/04/05/06/09/10/12/15/16/19/20 experiment, Option C (distinctive SINKFORGE treatment;
+## docs/handoff/ITM_VISUAL_EXPERIMENT.md). Where A lightens the well and B adds a category/state vocabulary
+## inside the same one-row bar, C changes the SILHOUETTE: three physical containers side by side -- a tool
+## rack, a material tray, a machine crate -- each with its own backing plate and its own pocket shape, so
+## "what kind of thing is this" reads from geometry before a player even looks at the icon. ITM-12's "UI
+## strip, not a carried kit" is the finding this option answers most directly.
+##
+## Fixed per-container capacity (3 tools / 5 materials / 2 machines, summing to
+## FactorySim.INVENTORY_SLOTS) is a deliberate limit of this option, not an oversight: a player carrying a
+## fourth tool or a sixth material type at once has no represented pocket for it (a small "+N" overflow
+## mark is drawn on that container instead of silently dropping the item). Neither other option has this
+## ceiling; see the report's "what remains unproven" for the real fix -- a per-container overflow scroll --
+## this bounded experiment does not attempt.
+const HOTBAR_TOOL_CAP_C: int = 3
+const HOTBAR_MATERIAL_CAP_C: int = 5
+const HOTBAR_MACHINE_CAP_C: int = 2
+const HOTBAR_PLATE_GAP_C: float = 10.0
+const HOTBAR_PLATE_PAD_C: float = 5.0
+const HOTBAR_TOOL_PLATE_C: Color = Color(0.16, 0.15, 0.14, 0.60)
+const HOTBAR_MATERIAL_PLATE_C: Color = Color(0.20, 0.17, 0.13, 0.48)
+const HOTBAR_MACHINE_PLATE_C: Color = Color(0.13, 0.15, 0.18, 0.60)
