+## The selected item's usability right now (ITM item/hotbar experiment, Options B and C's "unavailable"
+## state). Only a TOOL has a meaningful "can't act" reading in this bounded scope: whether the aimed cell is
+## something it can actually work, via `_workable`, the exact predicate mining already gates on -- not a
+## new rule. Materials and machines default to available; neither has an equivalently precedented
+## usability gate worth inventing for a presentation experiment.
+func _selected_item_available() -> bool:
+	var item: StringName = _selected_item()
+	if item == &"" or not MiningRules.is_tool_item(item):
+		return true
+	return _workable(_aim)
+
+
